Manual review pass. Corrections:

- Bare single-letter variable names in ordinary prose (exercise 1's "F" and
  "D", and "F"/"G" naming the two named vector fields in the C1/C2 problem
  group) were left as plain upright text by the converter instead of math
  mode. Hand-fixed to wrap each in $...$.

- Exercise 2 joined "a" and "b" across a single math span with
  \text{to} and manual \, spacing ($\mathbf{a}\,\text{to}\,\mathbf{b}$)
  instead of keeping "to" as ordinary prose between two separate math spans.
  Hand-fixed to "$\mathbf{a}$ to $\mathbf{b}$".

- Exercises 6 and 7 carried an empty superscript on the integral's lower
  limit ($\int_{C}^{}$), a redundant leftover from the MathML conversion.
  Hand-removed.

- Two curve labels with subscripts (C1/C2 introduced before exercise 27's
  group, and again where exercises 37-38 refer to F/G "over C1"/"over C2")
  were left as fragmented prose-plus-math, e.g. "C$_{1}$", instead of one
  math span. Hand-joined into $C_{1}$/$C_{2}$, matching how the file
  otherwise treats subscripted symbols (e.g. C$_{1}$'s own r$_1$/r$_2$
  neighbors elsewhere are figure-description labels, not math, and are
  left alone).

- Exercise 12 ("2y dx + 2x dy") and the differential in exercise 13's second
  term omitted the \, spacing before "dy" that the file uses consistently
  elsewhere ("2y\,dx" but "2xdy"; "]dy" instead of "]\,dy"). Hand-added the
  missing \,.

- Exercise 14's potential function had an extra brace around the last
  term's coefficient, {10y}^{2}, which changes the typeset meaning to
  (10y)^2 = 100y^2 rather than the intended 10y^2. Hand-removed the
  erroneous braces.

- Exercises 44 and 45 ("Calculate the line integral of F over C1", etc.)
  wrote both the field name and curve label in bare prose; joined with the
  F/G and C1/C2 fixes above.

- Exercises 44-45's two \dr integrals used unbolded "dr" ($\cdot\,dr$)
  instead of the file's consistent $d\mathbf{r}$ for the differential of a
  vector-valued position function. Hand-fixed both.

- Exercise 47's denominator carried a redundant outer brace pair around an
  already-parenthesized, already-superscripted group:
  \frac{...}{{(y^{2}+1)}^{2}}. A superscript attaches to the immediately
  preceding atom regardless of grouping, so "(y^{2}+1)^{2}" and
  "{(y^{2}+1)}^{2}" typeset identically, and the extra braces are noisier
  than the matching exponentiated-parenthetical elsewhere in this file.
  Hand-simplified to the braceless form.

- Exercise 49 (Earth/Sun gravitation problem) omitted the \, spacing before
  units ("10^{27}\text{g}", "10^{-8}\text{cm}", "10^{12}\text{cm}") that the
  same exercise's own last sentence ("$1\,\text{cm}$") and this file's unit
  conventions elsewhere use consistently. Hand-added the missing \,.

- Exercise 56 ("cos x cos y dx - sin x sin y dy") omitted the \, spacing
  before its second differential ("sin ydy" ran the variable and
  differential together), inconsistent with the \, before the first
  differential in the same integral. Hand-added the missing \,.

